    <div class="jnto-moe-ui-content-main jnto-moe-ui-story-detail">
      
  

  <div class="ct-header ct-header--slider ct-slick-custom-dots" id="jnto-moe-ui-hero-container">
  <div class="jnto-moe-ui-hero-slider" data-arrows="true" data-autoplay="true">
    
      
<div class="jnto-moe-ui-hero-item ct-header tablex item"
     data-background="https://res.cloudinary.com/parks-assets/image/upload/w_1650,f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,c_scale/v1/media_national_parks/filer_public/eb/27/eb270409-c111-47e1-89e3-16084e3ad69a/setonaikai_rokko-arima_ropeway_wtalz4">
  <div class="ct-u-display-tablex jnto-moe-ui-overlay">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-md-8 col-lg-12 slider-inner">
            <h3 class="big">Guides & Stories</h3>
            <h2 class="big">National Park in a City: Mount Rokko (Setonaikai)</h2>

            <p></p>
            
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

    
  </div>

  <div id="jnto-moe-ui-carousel-dots"></div>
</div>
  
  
<section class="jnto-moe-ui-section jnto-moe-ui-section-divider-top jnto-moe-ui-section-divider-white">
  <div class="jnto-moe-ui-visitor-center-section-content jnto-moe-ui-slim-wrapper">
    <div class="jnto-moe-ui-visitor-center-info">
      <p class="jnto-moe-ui-large-text">The Mount Rokko mountain range stands over the city of Kobe and offers a combination of culture, nature and recreation. Take a break from the city to explore beautiful Mount Rokko in Setonaikai National Park.</p>
      
        <p>Though its name may suggest otherwise, Mount Rokko is not a single peak, but rather a range of mountains overlooking the city of Kobe, defying common notions about the remoteness of national parks. Humans have shared close ties with the mountains for centuries. In ancient times, they were a sacred spot for ascetics and Buddhist monks. After Kobe&#39;s port opened to the world in the late 1800s, Mount Rokko became a recreational retreat for expats.</p>
      
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="jnto-moe-ui-visitor-center-section-content jnto-moe-ui-slim-wrapper">
    <div class="jnto-moe-ui-visitor-center-section-content">
      
      
        <p>Although the mountains were ravaged for their granite and timber in the past, being incorporated into Setonaikai National Park means they will continue to be preserved for generations to come. Today Mount Rokko sets an example for the coexistence of nature and city life. It has secluded nature trails, waterfalls and wildlife, alongside cable cars, modern art installations and the Rokko International Musical Box Museum. The mountains&#39; proximity to major train stations makes them easy to access and allow visitors to experience the riches of a national park while enjoying all the conveniences of a big city.</p>
      
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



